import lib/ui_native.dl
import tests/games/geometry_dash/session.dl

to paint a dash box at {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} sized {floating-point number:width} by {floating-point number:height} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    draw a flat UI box (UI box at x y sized width height) in ink on frame

to outline a dash box {UI bounds:box} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    paint a dash box at (box's x) (box's y) sized (box's width) by 2.0 in ink on frame
    paint a dash box at (box's x) (box's y + box's height - 2.0) sized (box's width) by 2.0 in ink on frame
    paint a dash box at (box's x) (box's y) sized 2.0 by (box's height) in ink on frame
    paint a dash box at (box's x + box's width - 2.0) (box's y) sized 2.0 by (box's height) in ink on frame

to paint a dash triangle from {UI point:first} through {UI point:second} to {UI point:third} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set color to the linear UI ink of ink on frame
    start triangles in frame
    add UI vertex first in color with alpha 255 to frame
    add UI vertex second in color with alpha 255 to frame
    add UI vertex third in color with alpha 255 to frame
    finish triangles in frame

to get dash point {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} about {floating-point number:cx} {floating-point number:cy} rotated {floating-point number:angle}:
    set radians to angle * 0.017453292519943295
    set cosine to the cosine of radians
    set sine to the sine of radians
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI point, cx + (x * cosine) - (y * sine), cy + (x * sine) + (y * cosine))

to paint dash face {UI bounds:box} about {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} rotated {floating-point number:angle} in {UI paint:ink} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set first to dash point (box's x) (box's y) about x y rotated angle
    set second to dash point (box's x + box's width) (box's y) about x y rotated angle
    set third to dash point (box's x + box's width) (box's y + box's height) about x y rotated angle
    set fourth to dash point (box's x) (box's y + box's height) about x y rotated angle
    paint a dash triangle from first through second to third in ink on frame
    paint a dash triangle from first through third to fourth in ink on frame

to paint dash cube {cube state:body} offset by {floating-point number:camera} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set x to body's x - camera + (the cube size / 2.0)
    set y to body's y + (the cube size / 2.0)
    set angle to body's rotation
    draw a UI disc at (@intrinsic("construct", UI point, x, y)) with radius 27.0 from (UI ink 172 255 51) to (UI ink 48 151 100) opacity 28 on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at -20.0 -20.0 sized 40.0 40.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 6 14 32) on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at -18.0 -18.0 sized 36.0 36.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 233 255 221) on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at -15.0 -15.0 sized 30.0 30.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 176 255 46) on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at -11.0 -9.0 sized 8.0 10.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 12 32 45) on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at 3.0 -9.0 sized 8.0 10.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 12 32 45) on frame
    paint dash face (UI box at -8.0 6.0 sized 16.0 5.0) about x y rotated angle in (UI ink 12 32 45) on frame

to paint the dash background for {dash session:session} offset by {floating-point number:camera} on {graphics frame:frame}:
    set phase to (session's tick as a floating-point number) * the dash tick
    set beat to ((phase * 2.25) - (the floor of (phase * 2.25)))
    set pulse to 1.0 - beat
    set tint to (1.0 + (the sine of (phase * 0.12))) / 2.0
    set top to UI ink between (UI ink 19 34 123) and (UI ink 53 23 132) at tint
    set bottom to UI ink between (UI ink 12 89 159) and (UI ink 38 62 160) at tint
    draw a rounded UI surface (UI box at 0.0 0.0 sized (the dash width) (the dash height)) with radius 0.0 from top to bottom opacity 255 feathered by 0.0 on frame
    set drift to (camera * 0.18) mod 192.0
    loop column from 0 to 8:
        set left to ((column as a floating-point number) * 192.0) - drift - 60.0
        set height to 132.0 + (((column * 79) mod 5) as a floating-point number) * 34.0
        paint a dash box at left (the dash floor - height) sized 112.0 by height in (UI ink between top and bottom at 0.43) on frame
        outline a dash box (UI box at (left + 12.0) (the dash floor - height + 12.0) sized 88.0 (height - 24.0)) in (UI ink between top and bottom at 0.65) on frame
    set drift to (camera * 0.35) mod 64.0
    set grid to UI ink between bottom and (UI ink 126 206 239) at (0.08 + pulse * 0.035)
    loop column from 0 to 22:
        paint a dash box at (((column as a floating-point number) * 64.0) - drift) 96.0 sized 1.0 by 514.0 in grid on frame
    loop row from 0 to 9:
        paint a dash box at 0.0 (98.0 + ((row as a floating-point number) * 64.0)) sized (the dash width) by 1.0 in grid on frame
    paint a dash box at 0.0 610.0 sized (the dash width) by 170.0 in (UI ink 4 13 39) on frame
    # Faint horizon stays decorative; only the obstacle table supplies support.
    paint a dash box at 0.0 610.0 sized (the dash width) by 2.0 in (UI ink 24 75 112) on frame
